{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>They trembled.</b> That they trembled from HaShem when they saw His might in the camp of Assyria, and they said: Who among us can dwell with HaShem, who is a consuming fire? And the meaning of 'in Zion' is that there the Glory is."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "Resolved ע השם as עם השם ('with HaShem'); the missing mem in the source may be a scribal abbreviation or defect."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:30.683324411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}